WEBVTT

00:12.167 --> 00:14.497
<i>The House of Tolui has fallen apart.</i>

00:20.757 --> 00:23.777
<b>6 Years Ago</b>

00:39.607 --> 00:41.307
It disappeared.

00:43.627 --> 00:46.697
Boraqchin! There you are!

00:47.577 --> 00:50.207
They've got all manner of gemstones
 on sale over there.

00:50.507 --> 00:51.677
Let's go take a look.

00:51.677 --> 00:52.727
Gemstones?

00:52.727 --> 00:56.867
Yep. I hear it's a caravan of traders
returned from the west.

00:56.867 --> 00:57.917
Off we go.

00:58.267 --> 01:03.337
I must decline. Gemstones 
would not look flattering on me.

01:05.997 --> 01:06.807
There.

01:07.847 --> 01:10.017
It's plenty fun just looking around.

01:16.787 --> 01:18.227
Hurry up!

01:37.837 --> 01:38.667
Take a look.

01:38.667 --> 01:42.007
Do you think these 
would make good earrings?

01:42.397 --> 01:44.007
They'd look splendid on you.

01:44.007 --> 01:47.007
You should pick something out
 as well, Boraqchin.

01:47.007 --> 01:49.817
No, like I said, I'm not...

02:01.777 --> 02:04.737
I wouldn't bother with that stone
 if I were you.

02:05.487 --> 02:09.787
That stone found its way 
into the gemstones we procured.

02:09.787 --> 02:13.997
It's a meddlesome stone 
that crumbles when exposed to light.

02:14.297 --> 02:16.267
It crumbles in light?

02:18.417 --> 02:24.137
<i>I was met with this shabby-looking stone 
amid the dazzling gemstones</i>

02:24.137 --> 02:26.487
<i>and took a strange fascination to it.</i>

02:27.287 --> 02:30.817
<i>That was how it all began.</i>

02:41.917 --> 02:44.607
<b>Jaadugar</b>

04:02.197 --> 04:07.817
<b>An Ungraceful Stone</b>

04:16.767 --> 04:18.627
It's coated in powder.

04:22.877 --> 04:28.207
After mere days of being exposed
 to sunlight, this hard stone...

04:29.147 --> 04:30.607
How strange.

04:34.177 --> 04:37.717
<i>After reading up on it, 
I learned this stone was called sandarac</i>

04:37.717 --> 04:41.147
<i>and was considered medicinal in the east.</i>

04:41.987 --> 04:46.837
<i>Taken in its proper dosage, it could heal
 abscesses and restore one's vigor.</i>

04:46.837 --> 04:47.777
<i>However...</i>

04:48.127 --> 04:52.977
<i>Heat it over a fire, and it turns 
to a white substance known as arsenic.</i>

04:54.067 --> 04:58.357
<i>A deadly poison that dissolves in water 
and is devoid of taste or odor.</i>

04:59.447 --> 05:02.787
This brittle stone unfit 
to become a gemstone...

05:03.047 --> 05:03.997
How...

05:04.407 --> 05:06.197
How fascinating.

05:07.217 --> 05:11.587
<i>The following year, 
Genghis Khan met his demise.</i>

05:12.167 --> 05:19.517
<i>Möge and I, who were his consorts, 
were taken as wives by our stepson Ögedei.</i>

05:20.017 --> 05:25.017
<i>And I became Ögedei's primary empress.</i>

05:26.877 --> 05:28.897
<i>Why did he choose me?</i>

05:29.357 --> 05:33.047
<i>I thought it was simply 
because I was the eldest.</i>

05:33.587 --> 05:34.567
<i>However...</i>

05:34.567 --> 05:38.157
Oh? A rock that crumbles in the light?

05:38.157 --> 05:39.867
Please pay it no mind.

05:39.867 --> 05:41.557
It is but a trifling hobby of mine.

05:42.747 --> 05:45.827
Your hobby does appear 
to be beyond my understanding.

05:46.177 --> 05:50.087
That said, I was happy to learn
 what it is you like.

05:50.947 --> 05:53.547
Please tell me if there's ever 
some other rock you want.

05:53.547 --> 05:54.987
I'll have it find its way to you.

05:54.987 --> 05:59.217
I will. But why do so much for me?

06:02.097 --> 06:03.977
The desire to obtain something.

06:04.797 --> 06:07.607
That urge is what sets 
the world in motion.

06:11.837 --> 06:17.697
I dream of this steppe becoming 
a vast market that connects east and west.

06:18.167 --> 06:23.207
People of eastern and western cultures 
alike passing through to do trade.

06:24.157 --> 06:27.647
That way, we won't need to venture off 
to wage war and plunder.

06:27.647 --> 06:30.307
People and goods 
will gather here willingly.

06:34.357 --> 06:37.387
I'd appreciate more stones, 
but books are what I want now.

06:37.917 --> 06:41.097
I'd like to learn more 
about the nature of these stones.

06:41.517 --> 06:42.807
Very well.

06:43.767 --> 06:47.697
I'm truly glad you became my empress.

06:48.807 --> 06:53.157
Tolui and the others would 
surely fail to grasp what I mean.

06:53.527 --> 06:58.047
That's why I want someone like you
 who <i>can</i> understand by my side.

07:04.707 --> 07:08.707
<i>The House of Tolui's power will 
deprive him of the ability to act freely.</i>

07:09.127 --> 07:11.617
<i>Can nothing be done about that?</i>

07:13.117 --> 07:16.817
Empress Boraqchin, 
your new physician is here to see you.

07:17.547 --> 07:18.847
Lady Möge has also come.

07:18.847 --> 07:20.297
Hey there.

07:21.267 --> 07:23.067
My word.

07:23.067 --> 07:27.717
I'm fond of rocks that change appearance
and behavior under heat or light.

07:28.227 --> 07:33.147
Eastern physicians like yourself 
are well-versed in these, yes?

07:33.147 --> 07:34.547
Indeed.

07:43.327 --> 07:47.887
There was a Daoist doctrine
 known as waidan.

07:47.887 --> 07:49.287
Waidan?

07:49.287 --> 07:53.507
Using fire or water to refine stones
much like the ones you have here,

07:53.507 --> 07:56.217
they tried to concoct immortality elixirs.

07:56.217 --> 08:00.897
However, inaccurate methods can result 
in a deadly poison instead.

08:01.217 --> 08:06.037
<i>It was at this moment that a plot 
began to formulate in my mind.</i>

08:14.157 --> 08:17.797
<i>That physician told me 
if I heated this powder,</i>

08:17.797 --> 08:20.757
<i>it would give me arsenic, 
which is lethal in minute doses.</i>

08:23.907 --> 08:27.877
<i>In its sandarac form, 
this shouldn't be enough to kill.</i>

08:28.567 --> 08:32.067
Unlike arsenic, it doesn't 
even dissolve in water.

08:32.627 --> 08:35.047
An ungraceful stone in every way.

08:36.307 --> 08:38.857
Why, you could say it's just like me.

08:53.727 --> 08:57.707
Huh. So this is the amount 
needed to cause this.

08:57.707 --> 08:59.857
Now, what remains is...

09:00.237 --> 09:02.177
<i>How to cure the ailment.</i>

09:02.997 --> 09:07.667
<i>Sandarac poison leaves the body 
after three months of recuperation.</i>

09:08.027 --> 09:12.367
<i>But was there no faster, 
more dramatic remedy?</i>

09:12.367 --> 09:14.707
<i>One that would seem like a miracle.</i>

09:15.797 --> 09:20.137
<i>That was when I met that girl.</i>

09:32.807 --> 09:34.207
<i>What do I do?</i>

09:34.627 --> 09:39.577
<i>One false move, and this plan 
will put the Great Kha'an's life in peril.</i>

09:50.467 --> 09:54.997
Why don't I entrust all of our fates 
in the hands of Tengri?

09:58.087 --> 10:01.207
I am to perform a divination.
One of you will accompany me.

10:10.797 --> 10:12.307
Here will do.

10:18.847 --> 10:20.527
Is everything ready?

10:20.527 --> 10:21.877
Um...

10:21.877 --> 10:25.067
Divinations need sheep bones,
and we don't have any.

10:25.067 --> 10:27.527
This fire isn't to heat up bones.

10:30.547 --> 10:31.787
Listen well.

10:31.787 --> 10:33.957
Cover your nose and mouth with a cloth.

10:33.957 --> 10:35.987
And don't stand downwind of the fire.

10:38.827 --> 10:41.707
What are you doing? 
Cover yourself at once.

10:41.707 --> 10:42.957
Y-Yes, ma'am.

10:51.787 --> 10:55.097
The red powder is turning white
 in the fire?

10:57.027 --> 10:58.057
A sign of good luck.

11:00.667 --> 11:04.967
<i>Sure enough, everything proceeded
 according to plan.</i>

11:18.107 --> 11:20.327
Just as I planned.

11:20.917 --> 11:22.167
Boraqchin.

11:23.327 --> 11:25.257
The Great Kha'an is here.

11:27.287 --> 11:29.387
Say, Boraqchin.

11:29.387 --> 11:32.007
Remember what you said to me?

11:32.397 --> 11:37.887
To ensure the Mongols are not divided, 
and our hearts remain as one...

11:37.887 --> 11:40.007
You said I should take action.

11:41.197 --> 11:44.227
Have I failed in doing so?

11:46.507 --> 11:49.627
Möge, you're fine just the way you are.

11:49.627 --> 11:51.977
As honest and as kind as ever.

11:52.467 --> 11:53.947
What's that mean?

11:54.807 --> 11:56.927
Don't you worry about a thing.

11:59.357 --> 12:02.457
If you say so, Boraqchin.

12:06.337 --> 12:07.507
<i>Möge.</i>

12:07.937 --> 12:10.777
<i>You don't need to concern yourself
 with any of this.</i>

12:11.127 --> 12:15.547
<i>This is a wager I've thrown myself into
 all on my lonesome.</i>

12:20.757 --> 12:23.457
I'm sorry I made you wait, Great Kha'an.

12:24.067 --> 12:26.107
What did you want to talk about?

12:26.107 --> 12:28.737
Yes, I have a proposal for you.

12:29.007 --> 12:33.487
It's about Tolui's widow, 
Sorghaghtani Beki.

12:34.607 --> 12:35.837
Get out already.

12:35.837 --> 12:36.697
I refuse.

12:36.697 --> 12:38.457
Please just leave us.

12:38.457 --> 12:40.807
I refuse! I'm sorry!

12:41.537 --> 12:46.107
I know you want to help Lady Töregene, 
but as you can see, today's not the day.

12:46.107 --> 12:47.487
No...

12:49.747 --> 12:50.797
H-Hey!

12:50.797 --> 12:52.187
Prince Güyük!

12:52.187 --> 12:56.177
Your mother also means 
a great deal to me.

12:56.177 --> 12:58.517
Please. If there's anything
 you can tell me...

12:59.537 --> 13:00.437
Hey.

13:02.227 --> 13:03.267
Someone's coming.

13:05.677 --> 13:06.727
Hey!

13:07.727 --> 13:11.267
That woman serves 
under Empress Boraqchin.

13:11.267 --> 13:14.197
We can't let her find out we're here.

13:14.197 --> 13:15.277
What do we do?

13:15.537 --> 13:17.097
That's the question.

13:18.907 --> 13:20.907
She's here! She's here!

13:41.507 --> 13:43.747
Good day to you, Prince Güyük.

13:44.197 --> 13:45.437
And to you, Sir Qadaq.

13:45.797 --> 13:48.707
I trust Lady Töregene 
is safe and sound?

13:48.707 --> 13:49.867
Why, of course.

13:49.867 --> 13:53.147
In fact, I've come to inform you
they're ready to release her.

13:58.517 --> 14:00.367
Pardon me. Continue.

14:01.007 --> 14:01.827
Right.

14:01.827 --> 14:04.707
However, there are a number of conditions.

14:05.057 --> 14:05.997
<i>Conditions?</i>

14:05.997 --> 14:09.087
First, Lady Töregene appears 
to be quite weary.

14:09.397 --> 14:13.337
She will spend her time quietly 
in Prince Güyük's territory from now on.

14:13.337 --> 14:15.797
<i>So they don't want her back 
in the emperor's court?</i>

14:16.147 --> 14:18.017
And one more thing.

14:18.017 --> 14:24.187
Prince Güyük is to marry Prince Tolui's
 first wife, Princess Sorghaghtani.

14:29.787 --> 14:32.077
We understand your conditions.

14:32.077 --> 14:34.357
Give us time to think it all over.

14:35.507 --> 14:40.177
Think carefully about what 
will be best for the Mongols.

14:41.327 --> 14:43.097
And with that, I bid you a good day.

14:48.747 --> 14:50.247
Good job holding out.

14:51.137 --> 14:51.837
Excuse me.

14:52.977 --> 14:54.667
About what she just said...

14:59.747 --> 15:04.097
In other words, this is all part
 of the Great Khatun's plot.

15:04.357 --> 15:07.287
Her aim is to diminish the power
 of the House of Tolui,

15:07.287 --> 15:10.227
and vest the Great Kha'an 
with greater authority.

15:11.197 --> 15:14.947
To accomplish this, she needed 
Prince Tolui to not simply perish,

15:14.947 --> 15:18.857
but to look like he sacrificed himself 
for the Great Kha'an.

15:20.367 --> 15:23.077
Does that mean 
the Great Kha'an's ailment...

15:23.077 --> 15:24.107
Yeah.

15:24.107 --> 15:27.267
She used Lady Töregene in her scheme
 to give him poison.

15:27.267 --> 15:28.787
One that wouldn't kill him.

15:28.787 --> 15:30.447
<i>Rahj al-gar.</i>

15:30.827 --> 15:34.167
<i>So she was testing the poison
 on herself for her plan.</i>

15:36.127 --> 15:39.227
<i>Using alchemy to orchestrate 
the lives and deaths of humans...</i>

15:40.557 --> 15:42.027
<i>As if she were a witch.</i>

15:43.727 --> 15:47.057
And she's even gotten 
Prince Güyük involved,

15:47.057 --> 15:48.977
making him marry 
Princess Sorghaghtani.

15:48.977 --> 15:50.687
There's nothing to object to, right?

15:50.687 --> 15:53.647
Doing so will bring back 
Lady Töregene as well.

15:56.877 --> 15:59.397
Well, it does serve our interests.

16:00.207 --> 16:01.567
S-Still...

16:02.107 --> 16:03.327
Prince Güyük!

16:03.667 --> 16:06.607
Please save Lady Töregene.

16:06.607 --> 16:07.457
I beg you!

16:15.087 --> 16:16.407
I'll do it.

16:21.007 --> 16:24.527
So long. I'm going to return
to Princess Sorghaghtani.

16:24.527 --> 16:25.717
Wait.

16:26.007 --> 16:28.567
Keep everything 
you've heard here a secret.

16:29.687 --> 16:31.007
I understand.

16:31.997 --> 16:33.567
I sure hope you do.

16:33.567 --> 16:35.217
You must be relieved, Fatima.

16:36.607 --> 16:39.027
Seems you'll be able to save
 the one you wanted to.

16:39.837 --> 16:40.617
Yeah.

16:43.347 --> 16:44.827
Thanks, Shira.

16:44.827 --> 16:46.947
It was reassuring having you with me.

16:47.337 --> 16:49.657
Y-Yeah, glad to hear it.

16:51.707 --> 16:54.247
May Allah preserve you.

16:54.567 --> 16:56.157
Make sure you keep it a secret.

16:56.157 --> 16:57.567
Yeah, yeah.

17:02.637 --> 17:04.097
What?!

17:04.097 --> 17:06.217
M-Mother? Marry Güyük?

17:06.217 --> 17:07.307
I won't hear of it!

17:07.557 --> 17:10.987
Yes. That's what I heard 
from the Great Khatun's messenger.

17:10.987 --> 17:14.027
I see the House of Ögedei 
has dropped all pretense.

17:14.027 --> 17:17.827
Not to mention, the lowly son of the sixth
empress is completely unfit to marry her.

17:17.827 --> 17:20.857
Still, it's what the Great Khatun wishes.

17:24.187 --> 17:25.327
I see.

17:25.327 --> 17:28.037
Mother! Don't tell me
 you plan to accept this.

17:28.507 --> 17:31.577
I refuse to call Güyük "Father."

17:33.517 --> 17:35.967
Mother? Mother!

17:35.967 --> 17:38.517
M-M-Mother!

17:38.517 --> 17:40.507
She seems pretty spiritless.

17:41.217 --> 17:44.827
Maybe I should've mentioned 
who killed Prince Tolui.

17:46.507 --> 17:49.677
I never thought Princess Sorghaghtani
 would remarry.

17:50.727 --> 17:54.517
The Great Kha'an and the House of Tolui 
will further join hands in the future.

17:55.057 --> 17:58.357
I was just about to send 
a messenger to Sorghaghtani.

17:59.527 --> 18:02.817
Then, please let me have the honor.

18:03.377 --> 18:04.787
You?

18:04.787 --> 18:05.527
Yes.

18:06.077 --> 18:11.777
You gave me the book I've wanted 
all this time as one born to scholars.

18:12.257 --> 18:14.617
I want to repay you for your kindness.

18:14.617 --> 18:15.687
Oh?

18:15.687 --> 18:18.407
I'm well-acquainted with the princess.

18:18.407 --> 18:20.767
I will manage to persuade her
 without fail.

18:21.407 --> 18:24.087
I see. How intriguing.

18:30.947 --> 18:33.727
<i>It's been three years 
since I last talked to her.</i>

18:33.727 --> 18:37.267
That is my role as the one 
who will one day be empress.

18:38.247 --> 18:40.887
<i>The same Princess Sorghaghtani,
reduced to this.</i>

18:41.367 --> 18:44.257
<i>How will she react when she sees me?</i>

18:44.587 --> 18:47.497
<i>Will she be justifiably angry? 
Will she berate me?</i>

18:48.707 --> 18:50.387
<i>That's fine by me.</i>

18:51.057 --> 18:56.027
<i>The anger I feel towards her
 burns far more intense.</i>

18:57.997 --> 18:59.407
Pardon me.

19:00.527 --> 19:04.007
Fatima? How long has it been?

19:04.007 --> 19:07.737
Indeed, Princess Sorghaghtani.

19:07.737 --> 19:10.717
I apologize for my long absence—

19:15.447 --> 19:18.817
<i>Shira did tell me that 
she was terribly despondent.</i>

19:22.247 --> 19:24.987
I'm here today as a messenger 
to the Great Khatun.

19:26.087 --> 19:30.447
I apologize for being unable 
to do anything for Prince Tolui.

19:30.447 --> 19:31.987
Pay it no mind.

19:37.237 --> 19:39.087
Please take a look at this.

19:39.747 --> 19:41.787
A gift from the Great Khatun.

19:43.207 --> 19:48.067
What's more, I come today to discuss 
a matter of great consequence.

19:48.547 --> 19:50.587
This matter I speak of...

19:51.097 --> 19:53.057
Please don't be alarmed.

19:53.377 --> 19:56.587
The Great Khatun asks 
that you marry Prince Güyük—

19:56.587 --> 19:58.547
I'll do as she says.

20:00.437 --> 20:03.647
If it will serve the Mongol people,

20:04.037 --> 20:07.107
do with me as you wish.

20:07.987 --> 20:10.487
<i>You can't be serious.</i>

20:13.537 --> 20:15.247
<i>You...</i>

20:15.247 --> 20:18.417
<i>You, who robbed me of everything...</i>

20:28.147 --> 20:30.427
<i>You, in all your arrogance...</i>

20:31.087 --> 20:34.727
<i>You've given up all hope 
after losing your loved one?</i>

20:42.197 --> 20:43.487
What's wrong?

20:44.637 --> 20:45.897
I admire your mind.

20:46.167 --> 20:48.857
<i>No. I need to look up at her.</i>

20:48.857 --> 20:50.947
<i>All I need to do is smile like always.</i>

20:50.947 --> 20:52.837
<i>Like I always do.</i>

20:56.447 --> 20:58.577
There's no one left to protect you.

21:03.697 --> 21:07.797
I-If you want to abandon all thought 
and yield to her, then suit yourself.

21:11.627 --> 21:15.497
But even though I've lost 
the ones I love...

21:16.327 --> 21:17.967
I will <i>never</i> give up hope.

21:20.157 --> 21:21.767
Stop your sulking.

21:22.207 --> 21:24.867
I'll keep thinking for myself.

21:30.397 --> 21:33.157
Translation: John K.
Timing: Andy Ellis
Editing: SMR
Quality Control: Alicia Ashby
Translation Check: Sriram Gurunathan

21:33.907 --> 21:36.307
Now for today's matter at hand:

21:36.307 --> 21:39.947
the remarriage of Princess Sorghaghtani
 to Prince Güyük.

21:40.257 --> 21:43.647
Sorghaghtani Beki has already consented.

21:44.077 --> 21:46.667
Prince Güyük, any objections from you?

21:53.567 --> 21:58.807
I hope this marriage forges a new bond 
between the Houses of Ögedei and Tolui.

21:59.517 --> 22:01.137
Heartwarming, indeed.

22:09.077 --> 22:13.487
<i>It was unwise to behave as I did 
to Princess Sorghaghtani.</i>

22:14.167 --> 22:17.487
<i>Well, I'm sure we won't ever meet again.</i>

22:36.587 --> 22:39.917
Finally, the date 
of the wedding ceremony will be—

22:39.917 --> 22:41.297
Please wait.

22:45.697 --> 22:49.067
Those preparations won't be necessary.

22:49.067 --> 22:51.107
P-Princess Sorghaghtani!

22:51.107 --> 22:52.107
Won't be necessary?

22:52.107 --> 22:54.107
What does she mean by that?

22:59.107 --> 23:00.537
<i>Oh, Tolui.</i>

23:01.207 --> 23:04.997
<i>I learned what it's like to lose someone
 for the first time.</i>

23:09.987 --> 23:11.897
<i>And to give up all hope.</i>

23:15.447 --> 23:17.417
<i>Oh, Tolui.</i>

23:19.247 --> 23:21.457
<i>Do you think this is how she felt?</i>

23:23.697 --> 23:28.227
My apologies, Great Kha'an. 
And to you, Great Khatun.

23:28.807 --> 23:33.067
I'm afraid I'll be declining 
this offer of marriage after all.

23:38.067 --> 23:43.257
<b>The Steppe, Ever Unchanging</b>

23:38.467 --> 23:42.127
<i>Next time: "The Steppe, Ever Unchanging."</i>
